despite being a company which prides  itself on making kids movies Disney is  responsible for some of the most  disturbing death scenes in cinema  history from tragic family lost to  straight-up body horror these are the  Disney deaths that traumatized us as  children considering so many Disney  characters tend to be orphans the lion  Kings Simba could be counted as lucky  this little lion cub has got a loving  mom and his father Mufasa is protective  gentle and understanding until he gets  trampled to death that is in the film's  darkest moments Simba finds himself  trapped in a gorge desperately trying to  outrun a herd of stampeding wildebeest  just when it looks like he's gonna wind  up as a pride land pancake Mufasa comes  to the rescue  leaping into the Horde of hooves and  horns to save his kid  but while Mufasa gets Simba to safety  climbing out of the gorge proves to be  too difficult for the mighty king  fortunately his dear old brother Skaar  is there to help while the film makes  clear that Mufasa has never been on  great terms with his brother there's  still a look of genuine betrayal on his  face when scar tosses him down to his  doom but the real heartache comes when  Simba tries to get his dad to wake up  nuzzling his lifeless body before  finally relenting and heading into exile  back in 1994 between the 1967 animated  classic and the 2016 remake Disney  released a live action version of the  jungle book the plot of the film has  Mowgli forced to lead a band of British  soldiers to a stash of hidden treasure  but as Mowgli and his sadistic captors  heading to the jungle this PG Kids flick  slowly transforms into a genuine horror  movie one villain falls from a cliff  another is mauled by a tiger while the  big bad eventually ends up in a watery  grave before being finished off by a  gigantic Python at one point a British  bully falls into a pit of quicksand and  despite his friends best efforts slowly  sinks into the muck crying in terror all  the way down another bat he finds  himself caught in a temple trap left  helpless as the roof seals shut and the  room fills with sand and to mean him for  all eternity  not exactly the bare necessities is it  despite the occasional moment of levity  the Hunchback of Notre Dom isn't afraid  to get dark with that said it should  come as no surprise that when the  villainous Claude Frollo meets his end  it comes in the most disturbing way  possible in the film's big finale  brolo is chasing the Hunchback Quasimodo  and his love Esmeralda through the halls  of Notre Dom hoping to catch and kill  the object of his desire the chase  eventually leads to the cathedrals  balcony and after a brief showdown this  happens  even kids can probably understand the  hellish metaphor and display here and  while Frollo does deserve his fate  watching him falling to the flames is  still enough to make anyone fear for  their immortal soul  the folks at Disney know there's nothing  scarier for a kid than the idea that  their mom could die that's one of the  reasons why Bambi is basically the  saddest animated movie ever made and  over 60 years later Pixar followed in  Bambi's hoof prints by traumatizing a  whole new generation with Finding Nemo  the movie opens on a hopeful note with  expectant parents Marlin and coral  moving into their oceanfront and nemenyi  home the two clownfish have over 400  little eggs waiting to hatch and they  couldn't be more excited about their  future that's when Marlin notices in  approaching Barracuda staring straight  at the parents and their unhatched kids  when the Barracuda moves in for the kill  Marlin does his best to ward off the  Beast but is knocked unconscious when he  wakes up coral is gone and every egg  save one has been devoured although we  don't actually see anyone get eaten we  do see poor Marlin mourn his dead wife  and unborn children his heartbreaking  sobs coupled with the idea you really  could lose your mom at any moments would  have made so many kids feel completely  adrift while watching the movie Davy  Jones is arguably one of the great  Disney villains thanks in large part to  a CGI face that still looks amazing  years after his appearance in the  Pirates of the Caribbean sequels with  his lobster hand tentacle chin and  supernatural crew Jones was a force to  be reckoned with  until the East India Trading Company got  a hold of his heart stashed away in a  wooden chest the heart gives the  villainous Cutler Beckett and his  henchman Ian Mercer the ability to  control the pirate lord near the end of  Pirates of the Caribbean at World's End  however Mercer finds out why you should  never play with a Buccaneers heart  during the film's climactic sea battle a  cannonball kills Mercer's men leaving  him alone with the octopus pirate  seizing the chance to reclaim his hearts  Jones kills Mercer in the slimy estroux  tzimmes way possible  it honestly might be the most gruesome  death in any Disney film ever  [Music]
 

